  "verified_mechanisms": [
    "Rust owns static palette text padding, preferred size, tight text bounds, escape border and search glyph. Native font metrics are cached and invalidate on text/theme changes. There are no hidden Labels outside the editor subtree in the Metal palette.",
    "Search, escape, hints and errors use four small Metal canvases sharing the existing device, queue and pipeline. The 32-byte GPU quad ABI is unchanged. The hint canvas is cropped to its text bounds so rounded corners, separator and native editor remain visible.",
    "Chrome updates independently of the result surface, including errors with an empty result list. Explicit text invalidation works under native paint lock, theme changes update scenes, and native recipe painting returns when Metal ownership is lost.",
    "Static text keeps native accessibility roles and names. The Textfield remains the only text-input owner; caret-only invalidations skip scene updates, while query/data changes explicitly schedule them.",
    "Rust provides the rounded frame and hint separator recipe; these still rasterize through the native compositor behind the editor. Native containers, window presentation, editing/IME and application services remain adapters.",
    "The default Views backend retains its direct Labels, glyph control and original padding/borders. All previous sidebar, split, palette and command regressions pass.",
    "The dedicated browser regression checks empty-result errors, editor/canvas non-overlap, tight hint bounds, AX names, missing native text painting while Metal owns the scene, fallback, theme updates, paint-lock error updates, invalid-scheme rejection and overlay cleanup."
  ],
